 "summary": "The SMT-LIB-based input format for syntax-guided synthesis problems: synth-fun declarations with a grammar restricting the candidate terms, declare-var universally quantified variables, constraint assertions over a background SMT theory, and check-synth; used by the annual SyGuS-Comp and solvers such as cvc5 and EUSolver.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "community-specification",
  "academic-paper"
 ],
